From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:21:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] software_isp: Calculate the statistics for every second
 frame

The autofocus waits for a statistics frame after every lens move, so with
statistics for only every fourth frame a focus step takes eight frames,
and a scan over the lens range takes several seconds. Statistics for every
second frame halve that. The AGC uses the exposure and gain of the frame
the statistics belong to, so it is not affected by the higher rate.
---
 include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swstats_cpu.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swstats_cpu.h b/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swstats_cpu.h
index abf2a60..8327695 100644
--- a/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swstats_cpu.h
+++ b/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swstats_cpu.h
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ public:
 	 * Run stats once every 4 frames to ensure any previous
 	 * exposure changes have been applied.
 	 */
-	static constexpr uint32_t kStatPerNumFrames = 4;
+	static constexpr uint32_t kStatPerNumFrames = 2;
 
 	bool isValid() const { return sharedStats_.fd().isValid(); }
 
